// Declarative syscall spec for plan9/arm -- deliberately EMPTY of
// //sys lines. Unlike Linux/Darwin, Plan9's own syscall ABI needs no
// shared _syscall6-style trampoline at all (see svc_arm.s's own header
// comment): every syscall here is either a hand-written raw stub
// directly under its real public name (open/close/pread/pwrite/seek/
// exits, in svc_arm.s) or a tiny C wrapper on top of one of those
// (read/write/exit, in syscall_plan9_arm.h below) -- there's nothing
// left for mksyscall.sh to generate. This file exists only so
// lib_core/libc/mkfile's existing, GOOS-generic generation rule
// (`syscall/os/$GOOS/zsyscall_${GOOS}_$cputype.c: syscall/os/$GOOS/
// syscall_${GOOS}_$cputype.decl`) has something to point at without
// needing a plan9-specific carve-out -- scripts/mksyscall.sh handles
// an empty decl input fine, producing a valid (just-the-includes) C
// file, which syscall_plan9_arm.h's own hand-written function bodies
// then get appended to via its #include.
